    "result_text": "The build is green. The audit log confirms the new identity in action: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers, with minimal structural impact \u2014 **2 files touched**, each change a small, self-contained unit.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote the single `service` method to build the new code:\n- `REGION` = region derived from the postcode via the existing `Locality.of(city, postcode)`.\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where `normalizedTelephone` reuses the existing `E164Telephone.toE164(...)`.\n- Removed the now-unused `OwnerRepository` param and the old `prefix3`/`countInCity` helpers.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 changed the `locality` mapping to derive from the new identity (the `REGION` prefix of `customerCode`) instead of re-deriving from `city`+`postcode`.\n\nThe other values built from `customerCode` moved automatically because they already read it:\n- **membership number** (`MembershipNumber.of(customerCode, \u2026)`) and **check digit** (`CheckDigit.of(customerCode)`) \u2014 untouched; now compute over the new code.\n- **create audit record** (`SaveOwner` logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`) \u2014 untouched; log line now shows `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\nI left `CheckDigit`/`MembershipNumber` (and their now-cosmetically-stale example comments) alone to avoid touching extra files, since their behavior follows the new `customerCode` string directly. Test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
